lesson: 256
title: Candles and party bags
level: primary-3
stars: 0
explain: A birthday cake has one candle for every year: a child turning 7 gets 7 candles.
explain: When several children have a cake each, add up their new ages to find all the candles.
explain: Cakes for children turning 5, 7 and 9: 5 + 7 + 9 = 21 candles.
vars: a=name b=name c=name x=2..12 y=2..12 z=2..12
need: x != y && y != z && x != z
answer: x + y + z
exercise: {a} is turning {x}, {b} is turning {y} and {c} is turning {z}. Each of them has a birthday cake. How many candles are needed in all?
exercise: Three cousins have birthday cakes this month. They turn {x}, {y} and {z}. How many candles go on the three cakes?
exercise: Mum bakes a birthday cake for each of her three children, who turn {x}, {y} and {z}. How many candles does she buy?
exercise: {a}'s cake is for {a.his} {x.ordwords} birthday, {b}'s for {b.his} {y.ordwords} and {c}'s for {c.his} {z.ordwords}. How many candles are on all the cakes?
exercise: At the club party there are cakes for three children turning {x}, {y} and {z}. How many candles are lit altogether?
exercise: 3 cakes, kids turning {x}, {y} n {z}. how many candles
exercise: {a}'s turning {x+1}, no wait {x}, {b} turning {y}, {c} turning {z}. candles for all of em?
exercise: buying candles for {a}, {b} n {c}'s cakes, they're turning {x} {y} {z}, the shop's shut at 5 btw. how many
exercise: my 3 cousins turn {x}, {y} and {z} this week lol, each gets a cake. how many candles total
exercise: we're doing cakes for {x}, {y} and {z} year olds birthdays. candles?
test: How many candles are needed for three birthday cakes when the children become {x}, {y} and {z} years old?
test: Three cakes stand on the table, one for each child's new age: {x}, {y} and {z}. Count the candles.
test: {c} lights the candles for {a}'s {x.ord}, {b}'s {y.ord} and {c.his} own {z.ord} birthday. How many candles does {c.he} light?
test: cakes for {x}, {y}, {z}. how many candles all up
test: {a} says {x}+{y}+{z} birthdays only need 3 candles lol. how many really
test: triple party, ages {x} {y} {z}, {b} brought {x} balloons too. how many candles
exam: It is given that three children attain the ages of {x.words}, {y.words} and {z.words} years respectively, each being presented with a birthday cake. Determine the aggregate number of candles required.
exam: Birthday cakes are to be prepared in respect of three persons attaining {x}, {y} and {z} years of age. Ascertain the total quantity of candles to be placed thereon.
exam: Compute the cardinality of the set of candles upon three birthday cakes, whereas the celebrants attain the ages of {x}, {y} and {z}.
exam: In respect of the birthday cakes of children turning {x}, {y} and {z}, one cake for each, state the total number of candles to be procured.
exercise: Grandma says she is twenty-nine again every year, so she gets no cake. {a} turns {x}, {b} turns {y} and {c} turns {z}, and each of them has a cake. How many candles are needed in all?
exercise: {a}'s {x}, {b}'s {y}, {c}'s {z}, and uncle Ron's not counting any more, vain old git, so no cake for him. candles for the three kids?
test: {a} was economical with the truth and told everyone {a.he} was turning {x+5}. Really {a.he} is turning {x}, {b} is turning {y} and {c} is turning {z}. Each true age is on a cake. How many candles are there?
